WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.894
Here is how to install Frog Bot on a Mac. One command does everything, and it takes about two minutes.

00:00:08.294 --> 00:00:16.282
First, open Terminal. Press Command and Space together, type Terminal, and press Enter.

00:00:16.682 --> 00:00:32.084
Go to the Frog Bot website and copy the Mac install command. Paste it into Terminal and press Enter. It downloads Frog Bot, puts it in your Applications folder, takes care of Mac security, and opens the app.

00:00:32.484 --> 00:00:39.153
Frog Bot opens on the sign in screen. The first time, click Create an account.

00:00:39.553 --> 00:00:49.745
Enter your name, your email, and a password of at least six characters. Then click Create account. Your team is private to your account.

00:00:50.145 --> 00:00:59.199
Next, paste your Claude or OpenAI API key, and click Start. Your key stays encrypted on your own computer.

00:00:59.599 --> 00:01:10.117
This is your team. Frog is your lead agent. Say hi, and tell it what you need, in plain words, like you would tell a coworker.

00:01:10.517 --> 00:01:20.940
Your name shows at the bottom left. Click it any time to change your picture, or to sign out. That is it. You are ready to go.

00:01:21.351 --> 00:01:27.164
Next time, open Frog Bot from Applications, or from Launchpad.

00:01:27.564 --> 00:01:38.687
If you downloaded the zip file instead, move Frog Bot to Applications, and run the command on screen once in Terminal. The install command does this for you.
